--- a/BUILDING.md
+++ b/BUILDING.md
@@ -12,6 +12,23 @@ libraries for SDL2 2.26+ (or SDL2-compat), libogg, libvorbis, libjpeg, and libpn
 - Windows: mingw-w64; host bootstraps vendored FPC and builds it locally, as with Linux by default. Requires quite a lot of memory (4+ gigs of RAM at minimum)
 - macOS: Xcode command-line tools and Homebrew (untested with this fork)
 
+On a Windows host the build provisions its own WinLibs under
+`.local/windows-host/winlibs/` and takes every tool from that one directory,
+never from `PATH`, so an unrelated MSYS2 or Visual Studio install cannot be
+mixed into a configure. A tree left by an older pin is replaced on next run.
+
+WinLibs is pinned to gcc 13.1.0 (POSIX threads) / mingw-w64 11.0.0 msvcrt r1,
+which bundles CMake 3.26.3 and Ninja 1.11.1: the newest release whose tools
+still start on Windows 7 SP1. CMake below 3.29 does not normalise separators in
+`-D` cache entries, so all paths handed to CMake use forward slashes; a
+backslash reaches `CMakeCCompiler.cmake` verbatim and fails the configure with
+`Invalid character escape`.
+
+That CMake asks Ninja for its version before every `try_compile`, so one launch
+that answers nothing stops a dependency configure; such a configure is retried
+while it keeps making progress. `SRHD_WINDOWS_GENERATOR=make` switches to the
+makefile generator, which is never probed.
+
 AVI playback needs Xvid: `libxvidcore.so.4` on Linux and `xvidcore` on macOS.
 `FPC_BOOTSTRAP` overrides the installed compiler used to bootstrap the pinned FPC.
 
